-- title:
--   Straight-line segments of the BSP construction block: init, dispatch and scan
-- statement:
--   Twenty-three straight-line facts about the program $\mathrm{bd}$ of definition `DetANN_HPIMBuildProg`: the start, the task dispatch, the end and the point scan.
--
--   Every conjunct has the same shape. Let $Q$ contain $\mathrm{bd}(o)$ at offset $o$ (`Embeds Q (bd off) off`), and let $s$ be a non-halted state at the stated pc with $1\le$ pointer 1 and the stated hypotheses. Then after exactly the stated number $t$ of steps, the run of $Q$ from $s$:
--   - is at the stated pc (relative to $o$) and has not halted;
--   - has the stated values in the changed registers and cells;
--   - leaves all other pointer and real registers and all other real and integer cells unchanged;
--   - has work $s.\mathrm{work}+t$, and its `cellsWritten` set consists of the listed cells.
--
--   Pointer 1 holds $m$, pointer 11 holds $n$, and $Z$, $R$ denote pointers 13, 14 of $s$.
--
--   1. **Init** $0\to13$ (13 steps): pointer $40:=Z$, $60:=2m$, $68:=1$, $69:=0$; reals $40:=r^2$, $41:=(cr)^2$, $47:=cr$, $49:=2r$, $50:=0$, $53:=2$ (with $r,c$ = reals 11, 12); pointers $14,43:=R-2m$ (the root box), $46:=0$.
--   2. **Copy step** $13\to13$ (7): when $i<2m$ ($i$ = pointer 46), real cell $p_{43}+i$ gets the value of $p_{17}+i$, and $i:=i+1$.
--   3. **Copy exit** $13\to20$ (1): when $i\ge2m$.
--   4. **Root task** $20\to34$ (14): pointers $59,44:=Z-1$ (the root slot), and the entry $[p_{43},Z-1,p_{40}]$ is pushed at $Z-4$; pointers $13,42:=Z-4$.
--   5. **Empty stack** $34\to395$ (1): when pointer $40\le$ pointer 42.
--   6. **End** $395\to396$ (1): pointer $17:=I[p_{59}]$.
--   7. **Pop** $34\to45$ (11): when the stack pointer $e$ (pointer 42) satisfies $e<p_{40}$: pointers $43:=I[e]$, $44:=I[e+1]$, $42:=I[e+2]$; the near box $q$: pointers $14,48:=R-2m$; flag $49:=0$, index $45:=0$.
--   8. **Scan exit** $45\to131$ (1): when $i\ge n$ ($i$ = pointer 45).
--   9. **Scan head** $45\to53$ (8): pointer 47 := the address of point $i$; reals $42,43:=0$; $46:=0$.
--   10. **Distance exit** $53\to86$ (1): when $j\ge m$.
--   11. **Distance step** $53\to53$ (33): adds the $j$-th terms of both squared distances (point at pointer 47, box at pointer 43) to reals 42, 43; $j:=j+1$.
--   12. **Far** $86\to126$ (3): when real $42>$ real 40 (which holds $r^2$ under `Env`).
--   13. **Good** $86\to128$ (4): when real $42\le$ real 40 and real $43\le$ real 41 ($(cr)^2$).
--   14. **Near, update** $86\to93$ (6): when near, not good, and the flag (pointer 49) exceeds pointer 69 (0).
--   15. **Near, first** $86\to116$ (6): when near, not good, and the flag is at most pointer 69.
--   16. **Update exit** $93\to126$ (1).
--   17. **Update step** $93\to93$ (23): coordinate $j$ of $q$ becomes $[\min(q_j,x_j),\max(q_{m+j},x_j)]$ for the point $x$.
--   18. **First step** $116\to116$ (9): coordinate $j$ of $q$ becomes $[x_j,x_j]$.
--   19. **First exit** $116\to126$ (2): flag $49:=1$.
--   20. **Next point** $126\to45$ (2): $i:=i+1$.
--   21. **Certified leaf** $128\to383$ (3): pointer $61:=i+1$.
--   22. **No near point** $131\to383$ (2): when the flag is 0: pointer $61:=0$.
--   23. **Near points** $131\to134$ (3): when the flag is 1: pointers $46:=0$, $61:=0$.
